  "full_text": "So just in the backyard for actually I think God does anything for fun I don't really do anything for fun. Wait, because that's no fun. You know one time I was asking God I said Don't angels get bored? Why do they like pay attention to humans? God said we like bored Wait, I guess if you've been alive a billion years If you've survived that, then you can obviously survive boredom, you know? You think there's any kind of a proof that if you've been alive for a billion years, you gotta be bored? I figured out what song was in my head. Gates. God's will in ways. As the deer pants for the waters, Brooks, so my soul pants for you, oh God. Godliness is something below the surface of a life, deep down in the realm of attitude, an attitude towards God himself. The longer I think about this, the more I believe that a person who is godly is one whose heart is sensitive towards God, one who takes God seriously. The godly individual hungers and thirsts after God. The word of the psalmist is, the godly person has a soul that, quote, pants for the living God. Godly people possess an attitude of willing submission to God's will in ways. Whatever he says goes, and whatever it takes to carry it out is the very thing the godly desire to do.",
